{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghbf3HgiRQzPUnCeDLPr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Dq ≈ 427 cm⁻¹ (Δt = 10Dq ≈ 4 270 cm⁻¹) and B ≈ 899 cm⁻¹.**\n\n**Method.** A tetrahedral d⁸ ion has the same term ordering as an octahedral d² ion. The ground state is ³T₁(F). The three spin-allowed bands are ³T₁(F) → ³T₂, ³A₂ and ³T₁(P). I fitted the three bands with the octahedral d² model, using Dq as the magnitude of the tetrahedral Dq. The fit used the `ts_fit_spectrum` tool.\n\n**Assignment and fit.**\n\n| Band | Observed (cm⁻¹) | Calculated (cm⁻¹) |\n|---|---|---|\n| ν₁, ³T₁ → ³T₂ | 3 600 | 3 598 |\n| ν₂, ³T₁ → ³A₂ | 7 870 | 7 871 |\n| ν₃, ³T₁ → ³T₁(P) | 16 410 | 16 410 |\n\nThe residuals are 2 cm⁻¹ or less, and the fit's rmse is about 1.2 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Hand check.** The ³A₂ and ³T₂ terms are not mixed with other terms, so ν₂ − ν₁ = 10Dq. That gives 4 270 cm⁻¹, so Dq = 427 cm⁻¹, matching the fit. A quick hand solution for B using only the T₁ mixing matrix was not self-consistent. I did not resolve that discrepancy and rely on the tool fit for B.\n\n**Racah C.** The tool also reports C = 3 801 cm⁻¹. This is the tool's default, not a fitted result. The spin-allowed bands of d⁸ do not depend on C, so these three bands cannot determine it. I therefore leave C out of the answer.\n\nB ≈ 899 cm⁻¹ is about 87% of the free-ion value for Ni²⁺ (about 1 040 cm⁻¹). The free-ion figure is a recalled literature value, not computed here. This indicates moderate covalency.\n\n{\"Dq\": 427, \"B\": 899, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Tetrahedral d8 maps onto the octahedral d2 manifold; the three spin-allowed bands fit with rmse about 1 cm^-1, and C is not determined by these bands.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2702,"cache_read_input_tokens":7975,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens